      "dramatis_personae": "- **The Triad of Repression (`MYB3R1`, `MYB3R3`, `MYB3R5`):** Three redundant R1R2R3-Myb transcription factors acting as the active executioners of cell cycle arrest. They bind to the promoters of mitotic genes to lock them down.\n- **Squad myb3r135 (The Defiant Mutants):** Triple knockout seedlings lacking all three repressors. When hit by radiation, they refuse to stop dividing, dragging broken chromosomes into catastrophic mitotic division.\n- **Squad Col-0 (The Prudent Sentinel):** Wild-type seedlings deploying the MYB3R triad to enforce an ironclad G2-phase quarantine.\n- **The Target MSA Box (`5'-AACGG-3'`):** M-Specific Activator cis-elements located in the promoters of G2/M genes where the MYB3R repressor complex docks.\n- **The Bypassed Mitotic Engines (`CYCB1;1`, *Cyclin B1;1*, `KNOLLE`):** Genes that are silenced in wild-type plants but remain aberrantly active in *myb3r135*.\n- **Dr. Arp Schnittger & Dr. Kengo Kobayashi:** Molecular cytogeneticists investigating how cells enforce mitotic discipline under high-energy particle bombardment.",
      "script_markdown": "### Act I: The Mutants That Refused to Stop (Pages 1–10)\n\n**Page 1**\n- **Panel 1 [Wide Shot]:** Inside the radiation imaging lab. Two rows of seedlings sit side by side: wild-type Col-0 and the `myb3r135` triple mutant. Both have just received a 10 Gray dose of gamma radiation.\n- **Panel 2:** Fluorescence microscopy of root apical meristems. In Col-0, mitotic figures vanish; all cells arrest in interphase. In `myb3r135`, cells continue dividing frantically!\n- **Caption (Narrator):** *When a human cell detects broken chromosomes, it freezes to heal. If it cannot stop, it becomes cancerous or dies. In plants, the brake pedal is a triad of three Myb proteins: MYB3R1, MYB3R3, and MYB3R5.*\n- **Dialogue (Cytogeneticist):** \"Look at the *myb3r135* root tips! They aren't pausing! Cells are entering anaphase with shattered chromatids! Chromosome bridges are forming everywhere!\"\n\n**Page 2**\n- **Panel 1:** Cutaway into the promoter of *CYCB1;1*. In wild-type Col-0, the MYB3R repressor complex binds to the `AACGG` MSA box, recruiting histone deacetylases (*HDA6*) to condense chromatin into a closed, silent conformation.\n- **Panel 2:** In the `myb3r135` mutant, the MSA box is empty. Transcription factors (*MYB3R4*, an activator) continue loading RNA Polymerase II, driving cyclin synthesis forward.\n- **SFX:** *KRRR-BREAK (Anaphase chromosome tearing)*\n- **Dialogue (Dr. Schnittger):** \"The repressor complex is gone! The cells can't see the stop sign! They're replicating right through the double-strand breaks!\"\n\n**Page 3**\n- **Panel 1:** Cytogenetic karyotype view of dividing cells. In Col-0, chromosomes are intact after repair. In `myb3r135`, chromosome fragments are left behind in the cytoplasm, forming aberrant micronuclei.\n- **Panel 2:** Micronuclei rupture, triggering cytoplasmic DNA sensors and causing necrotic lesions across the root elongation zone.\n- **Caption:** *Stopping is not a failure of growth. Stopping is the ultimate survival strategy.*\n\n**Page 4–10**\n- RNA-Seq analysis of `myb3r135` vs. Col-0 under radiation.\n- Discovery: Over 350 mitotic G2/M genes fail to be downregulated in the triple mutant!\n- *CYCB1;1*, *CYCA2;1*, *CDKB2;1*, *KNOLLE*, and *AURORA1* remain expressed at 80% to 100% of non-irradiated levels.\n- Meanwhile, DNA repair genes (*RAD51*, *BRCA1*) are still induced normally via SOG1, proving that **SOG1 activation and MYB3R repression operate as two distinct, parallel arms of the damage response**!\n\n### Act II: The DREAM Complex Analogy (Pages 11–20)\n\n**Page 11–15**\n- Molecular architecture of the plant DREAM-like repressor complex:\n  - MYB3R proteins assemble with E2F-DP transcription factors (*E2FB*, *DPA*) and retinoblastoma-related protein (*RBR1*).\n  - This multimeric complex represses E2F- and MSA-regulated genes simultaneously.\n- In *myb3r135*, the complex falls apart, unlocking the entire mitotic cell cycle engine.\n\n**Page 16–20**\n- Rescue experiments:\n  - Reintroducing *MYB3R3* alone into the triple mutant restores 70% of the G2/M arrest phenotype, proving that the three members act redundantly.\n  - *MYB3R3* acts as the primary heavy-duty repressor, while *MYB3R1* and *MYB3R5* fine-tune tissue-specific responses.\n\n### Act III: The Radiation-Hardened Crop Strategy (Pages 21–32)\n\n**Page 21–25**\n- Application for deep-space agriculture:\n  - Can we engineer space crops with hyper-active MYB3R complexes?\n  - Overexpression of *MYB3R3* under a radiation-inducible promoter (*pRPA1A::MYB3R3*) produces \"super-checkpoint\" plants that halt division at the slightest whisper of radiation, repair all damage, and resume growth with zero mutations.\n\n**Page 26–30**\n- Final debrief: Integrating the activator (SOG1) and the repressor (MYB3R) into a single unified model.\n- Closing panel: An astronaut looking through the glass of a lunar greenhouse, holding a vibrant green seedling whose cell cycles pause gracefully under cosmic rays and resume with flawless genomic purity.\n\n**Page 31–32**\n- Infographic spread: The MYB3R Repressor Circuit and MSA Promoter Occupancy Model.",
